  <Patch Id="G3T2wnJ1ojC5ZLXDL8sPRr">
    <Canvas Id="KYtgwhsmi9nn50bFBLe3uz" DefaultCategory="Main" CanvasType="FullCategory" />
    <Node Name="Application" Bounds="100,100" Id="QjGUp0aIeDMzV9uCJeP5fr">
      <p:NodeReference>
        <Choice Kind="ContainerDefinition" Name="Process" />
        <FullNameCategoryReference ID="Primitive" />
      </p:NodeReference>
      <Patch Id="QPk2GpRtKNJoXr2Vxvh3lF">
        <Canvas Id="VMPnBGp1UQjM8aKDG3eXNd" CanvasType="Group">
          <Pad Id="TOtzkLzuwpohhHa0boXNo5" Bounds="-800,-60,660,620" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="ACT IV LAB - Experiment: the globe, stage 0. NOT a shipped unit. Direction and evidence: docs/GLOBE-RESEARCH.md.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;THE QUESTION: can the 2D map VL.Mapsui already draws be wrapped onto a sphere in Stride, with zero new nodes?&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;WHAT IS HERE. Left column: the map you know from Prompt Paint by numbers - 177 countries from one public-domain file, painted by log10(population) between two teals, a graticule on top, no tiles, no network. Its Map is parked at zoom 4, centre 0,0: at 4096 x 4096 pixels that is EXACTLY the whole Web Mercator square (16 x 16 tiles of 256 px, 9.8 km per pixel at the equator).&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Right column: vvvv's own SkiaTexture turns ToSkiaLayer into a Stride texture; a ShaderFX node (lab/shaders/MercatorUV_ShaderFX.sdsl, ten lines) remaps the sphere's texture coordinates so that Stride's equirectangular Sphere reads a Mercator picture without distortion; the sampled colour goes out as Emissive, so no light is needed. Drag in the Stride window to orbit; wheel to zoom.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;WHAT TO LOOK FOR (rung 4 - the picture is the control):&#xD;&#xA;- continents in the right places and the right way round (a mirrored Africa means u needs flipping in the shader);&#xD;&#xA;- the graticule's meridians converging at the poles, parallels evenly spaced in LATITUDE (if they bunch toward the poles, the remap is not running);&#xD;&#xA;- a flat cap above 85 degrees - Web Mercator has no poles; the sampler clamps;&#xD;&#xA;- zoom in: the picture goes soft at about 10 km per pixel. That is the ceiling of a single-texture globe, and the argument for stage 2 (one patch per tile), not for a bigger texture.&#xD;&#xA;- DIAGNOSTICS on prints Mapsui's viewport size onto the texture; it must read 4096 x 4096.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Rules of the lab: no new library surface (every node here shipped already; the shader is a text file beside this document), nothing fetched, results recorded in docs/ACT-IV-LAB.md. Data: Natural Earth 110m countries (public domain), row in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md.">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">11</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="HUKU5uHdUpkQnp5aTWIX8r" Comment="File Path" Bounds="60,0,320,15" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="..\help\Assets\countries-population.geojson">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="IO" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="Path" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
          </Pad>
